{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "01VL", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{L}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{L}$", "MATH_0005": "$f$", "MATH_0006": "$X/S$", "MATH_0007": "$f$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{O}_S$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{E}$", "MATH_0010": "$i : X \\to \\mathbf{P}(\\mathcal{E})$", "MATH_0011": "$S$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{L} \\cong i^*\\mathcal{O}_{\\mathbf{P}(\\mathcal{E})}(1)$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0003": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0004": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0003": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0004": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-very-ample}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:c7713ef3505aaac724f5355f83230bd7c0c0fe73f2941d23b99a264621fe2b40", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:821dd4d725da759464dfbac2fa4139515f90fc59d9853af540faf10bfb61a428", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes.\nLet <MATH_0002> be an invertible <MATH_0003>-module.\nWe say <MATH_0004> is <TEXTITOPEN_0001>relatively very ample<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> or more\nprecisely <TEXTITOPEN_0002><MATH_0005>-relatively very ample<TEXTITCLOSE_0002>, or\n<TEXTITOPEN_0003>very ample on <MATH_0006><TEXTITCLOSE_0003>, or <TEXTITOPEN_0004><MATH_0007>-very ample<TEXTITCLOSE_0004> if\nthere exist a quasi-coherent <MATH_0008>-module\n<MATH_0009> and an immersion <MATH_0010>\nover <MATH_0011> such that\n<MATH_0012>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b438d16dc38c9fa5c3eb08695b6e8f17251984b80c226e382b002a6b2720cb9e", "unit_id": "tag:01VM:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01VL", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:eddfaba6948ec9ae6cdc64ab2f988ee461f8db399613993df27800d7119dbddd", "source_text": "\n\n\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nSince there is no assumption of quasi-compactness in this definition it is not\ntrue in general that a relatively very ample invertible sheaf is a relatively\nample invertible sheaf.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a8e7d0802ddd8c6cb401689aab030cc3ea8b524a8a00abd04ab0fa977b9f6959", "unit_id": "tag:01VL:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01VL", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\begin{reference}\n\\cite[II, Proposition 4.6.2]{EGA}\n\\end{reference}", "MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{L}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0004": "$f$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{L}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{L}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-ample-very-ample}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:4ac300b9ef7bcd388afc52a785a4512d682b91b255921bdbf76cf8683c3a27a1", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2891cfbe0ca118bc6076343bdfde53a8fa21461138955bb1c986fd784a9daf4e", "source_text": "<LOCKED_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes.\nLet <MATH_0002> be an invertible <MATH_0003>-module.\nIf <MATH_0004> is quasi-compact and <MATH_0005> is a relatively\nvery ample invertible sheaf, then <MATH_0006> is a relatively\nample invertible sheaf.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8f0d6731ffb7935e9ac1fb72c160d12ab2696f9beeb8a9fc381b0a08b0185d85", "unit_id": "tag:01VN:statement"}
